{
 "turns_text": [
  "[SEG0001] person_1 (NURSE): Elaine, come through. He's just sorting something on the computer, won't be a tick.",
  "[SEG0002] person_2 (PATIENT): Thanks love. That waiting room telly was on some auction thing, I nearly bought a vase in my head.",
  "[SEG0003] person_3 (DOCTOR): Mm. Sorry. Right. What brings you in?",
  "[SEG0004] person_2 (PATIENT): My jaw. It hurts when I chew, right side, quite sharp.",
  "[SEG0005] person_3 (DOCTOR): How long's that been happening?",
  "[SEG0006] person_2 (PATIENT): We were just saying, weren't we, the 47 was a nightmare this morning, standing room only, and then the dog next door...",
  "[SEG0007] person_4 (CAREGIVER): Elaine, he's asking about the jaw, not the bus.",
  "[SEG0008] person_3 (DOCTOR): Yes, sorry, say again how long the pain's been there. I lost you.",
  "[SEG0009] person_2 (PATIENT): Umm, about three weeks. Maybe a shade longer. It kicked off after that stocktake at work.",
  "[SEG0010] person_3 (DOCTOR): And is there a click?",
  "[SEG0011] person_2 (PATIENT): Oh there is, a little pop when I open wide. Gets worse when I'm stressed, which, well, the stocktake nearly finished me.",
  "[SEG0012] person_4 (CAREGIVER): She's grinding her teeth at night. I hear it through the wall, sounds like she's chewing gravel.",
  "[SEG0013] person_3 (DOCTOR): Grinding. Ok. Hold on, this box has popped up. Any temperature, any fever with it?",
  "[SEG0014] person_2 (PATIENT): The chemist on the corner shut early yesterday, that's why I couldn't get...",
  "[SEG0015] person_3 (DOCTOR): Fever. Have you had a fever?",
  "[SEG0016] person_2 (PATIENT): No. No fever. I've felt alright in myself.",
  "[SEG0017] person_3 (DOCTOR): Headaches?",
  "[SEG0018] person_2 (PATIENT): No, no headaches.",
  "[SEG0019] person_3 (DOCTOR): Any change in your eyesight, blurring, that sort of thing?",
  "[SEG0020] person_2 (PATIENT): Eyes are fine. I had them tested in March for the reading glasses, but that's separate.",
  "[SEG0021] person_3 (DOCTOR): Scalp tender when you brush your hair?",
  "[SEG0022] person_2 (PATIENT): No, nothing like that. My hairdresser's on holiday actually, which is a pain because...",
  "[SEG0023] person_4 (CAREGIVER): She's not had a sore scalp.",
  "[SEG0024] person_3 (DOCTOR): Right. Pain only with chewing, or sitting there as well?",
  "[SEG0025] person_2 (PATIENT): Chewing mostly. Toast is awful. It aches in the evening if I've been clenching all day.",
  "[SEG0026] person_3 (DOCTOR): Sorry, the aching, say that once more.",
  "[SEG0027] person_2 (PATIENT): Evening ache if I've clenched. Chewing is the sharp bit.",
  "[SEG0028] person_1 (NURSE): Sorry to butt in. Her obs from just now, temperature 36.8, pulse 76, blood pressure 142 over 86.",
  "[SEG0029] person_3 (DOCTOR): Ta. Open your mouth for me a second. Yes, I can feel a click over the right joint. Temples aren't tender. I can't see any swelling along the gum.",
  "[SEG0030] person_2 (PATIENT): Is that bad? My aunt had her teeth out and she said the dentist was ever so rough, mind you that was years ago in Leeds.",
  "[SEG0031] person_3 (DOCTOR): What medicines are you on at the moment?",
  "[SEG0032] person_2 (PATIENT): I was going to say, the garden centre has those plugs on offer, I nearly went after this.",
  "[SEG0033] person_3 (DOCTOR): Medicines. What do you take?",
  "[SEG0034] person_2 (PATIENT): Ibuprophen, the 400 milligram tablets, when the jaw really bites. Usually twice a day the last week or so.",
  "[SEG0035] person_4 (CAREGIVER): And her blood pressure tablet every morning.",
  "[SEG0036] person_3 (DOCTOR): Which one, and the dose? I can't see it loading.",
  "[SEG0037] person_2 (PATIENT): Err, ramapril, five milligrams, once in the morning. Years now, for the blood pressure.",
  "[SEG0038] person_3 (DOCTOR): Anything else you've tried for the jaw?",
  "[SEG0039] person_2 (PATIENT): Paracetamol for a few days. Didn't touch it, so I stopped.",
  "[SEG0040] person_3 (DOCTOR): Ok. This is most likely the jaw joint from the grinding, the temporomandibular joint, but at your age I can't completely rule out artery inflammation, so I want some bloods.",
  "[SEG0041] person_2 (PATIENT): Artery? That sounds grim. I only came about the chewing.",
  "[SEG0042] person_3 (DOCTOR): It's a precaution. Nurse will take bloods Thursday morning, an ESR and a CRP. No need to fast, just come Thursday morning.",
  "[SEG0043] person_1 (NURSE): I'll put her in for Thursday morning, half eight, with me.",
  "[SEG0044] person_3 (DOCTOR): If those are borderline we'll do an ultrasound of the temporal artery. And if the jaw does not settle, then a scan.",
  "[SEG0045] person_2 (PATIENT): A scan. Do I need to, umm...",
  "[SEG0046] person_3 (DOCTOR): Not now. Soft foods for a couple of weeks, nothing chewy. And get a soft mouth guard from the chemist, wear it at night.",
  "[SEG0047] person_4 (CAREGIVER): I'll make sure she puts it in. She'll forget otherwise.",
  "[SEG0048] person_2 (PATIENT): I won't forget. Well, I might. The dog was at it again and I was going to tell you...",
  "[SEG0049] person_3 (DOCTOR): I'll see you back in two weeks with the results.",
  "[SEG0050] person_2 (PATIENT): Two weeks. Shall I bring the mouth guard so you can see it?",
  "[SEG0051] person_3 (DOCTOR): Yes, bring it with you. If your eyesight changes or the pain turns sudden and severe before then, don't wait, go to A and E.",
  "[SEG0052] person_2 (PATIENT): A and E. Right. I hope it doesn't come to that. I've got a library shift Thursday afternoon, is morning alright?",
  "[SEG0053] person_3 (DOCTOR): Morning's fine, bloods first. I need to sort this screen. Off you go."
 ],
